  "wikitext": "{{Short description|Species of flowering plant}}\n{{italic title}}\n{{Speciesbox\n|name = Heath milkwort\n|image = Polygala serpyllifolia.jpg\n|genus = Polygala\n|species = serpyllifolia\n|authority = Hosé\n}}\n\n'''''Polygala serpyllifolia''''', the '''heath milkwort''', is a European native perennial of heaths and grassy places.\n\n==Description==\nIt grows to a height of 25&nbsp;cm. The lower leaves are in opposite pairs. It flowers from May to August.\n\n==References==\n{{Reflist}}\n*''Wild Flowers of Britain'' by Roger Phillips.\n\n{{Taxonbar|from=Q162400}}\n\n[[Category:Polygala|serpyllifolia]]\n\n\n{{Polygalaceae-stub}}",
